    {
      "id": "1573542934761181315",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-21T03:37:50.661+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": true,
      "content": "# Welcome to #\uD83C\uDFB6-eurosynth\n**EuroSynth** is @Andrew Wingate's synthesizer on a chip: a complete eurorack synth voice, built entirely in digital logic and made on wafer.space Run 2 as [EURO](<https://wafer.space/ws-run2/projects/EURO.html>). Andrew looks after this channel.\n\nYou can hear it before you hold one. The [live playground](<https://anfroholic.github.io/eurosynth/web/>) runs the chip's exact reference models in your browser, so what you hear is what the silicon produces.\n\nTo dig in, start with the [showcase](<https://github.com/anfroholic/eurosynth/blob/main/docs/SHOWCASE.md>), then read the [hardware guide](<https://github.com/anfroholic/eurosynth/blob/main/docs/HARDWARE_GUIDE.md>) when you're ready to build a board. The source is at [anfroholic/eurosynth](<https://github.com/anfroholic/eurosynth>).\n\nGot a chip? Share your boards, patches, recordings and questions here.",
